<p:notes xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:p14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/powerpoint/2010/main" xmlns:p15="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/powerpoint/2012/main" xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr>        <p:cNvPr id="1" name=""/>        <p:cNvGrpSpPr/>        <p:nvPr/>      </p:nvGrpSpPr>      <p:grpSpPr>        <a:xfrm>          <a:off x="0" y="0"/>          <a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/>          <a:chOff x="0" y="0"/>          <a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/>        </a:xfrm>      </p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="206" name="PlaceHolder 1"></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="sldImg"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="685800" y="1143000"/><a:ext cx="5486040" cy="3085920"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:ln w="0"><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="207" name="PlaceHolder 2"></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="body"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="685800" y="4400640"/><a:ext cx="5486040" cy="3600000"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln w="0"><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr lIns="91440" tIns="45720" rIns="91440" bIns="45720" anchor="t"><a:noAutofit/></a:bodyPr><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" algn="l"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t>Preview 6 and Preview 7 gave dotnet test more attention than it usually receives in headline summaries. Preview 6 added options and output improvements and updated templates for xUnit version 3 and NUnit on Microsoft.Testing.Platform. Preview 7 added a run-level timeout and a maximum-failed-tests threshold. These controls are valuable in CI because they prevent a hung or catastrophically failing run from consuming an entire agent window. Traversal project support helps repositories that use Microsoft.Build.Traversal to coordinate many projects from a single entry point. Reporter improvements make test outcomes easier to understand. MAUI device and environment support also broadens the testing model. Teams may already implement similar behavior in pipeline YAML or wrapper scripts. The opportunity is to simplify that automation by moving common controls into the standard CLI. Before changing a pipeline, compare exit codes, result files, cancellation behavior, parallelism, and how the CI system surfaces failures. Standardization helps only when observability remains at least as good.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" algn="l"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t>Sources:</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" algn="l"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="000000"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst></a:effectLst><a:uFillTx/><a:latin typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t>https://devblogs.microsoft.com/dotnet/dotnet-11-preview-6/</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="0" u="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgb